      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-184005",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose we wish to construct a direct proof of the following statement:\n\n> If $n$ is an even integer, then $3n + 2$ is even.\n\nA proof schema is outlined below. Fill in the missing entries.\n\nLet $n$ be an {{field-1}} integer. Then, $n =$ {{field-2}} for some integer $a$.\n\nSubstituting {{field-3}} into the expression $3n + 2$, we can show that $3n + 2 =$ {{field-4}}, where $b$ is {{field-5}}.\n\nTherefore, since $3n + 2$ {{field-6}} a multiple of $2$, we conclude that $3n + 2$ is {{field-7}}."
