      ":question/problem": "Suppose we wish to construct a direct proof of the following statement:\n\nIf $n$ is an even integer, then ${n}^{3}+2n$ is even.\n\nA proof schema is outlined below. Fill in the missing entries.\n\nLet $n$ be an {{field-1}} integer. Then, $n=$ {{field-2}} for some integer $a.$\n\nSubstituting {{field-3}} into the expression ${n}^{3}+2n$, we can show that ${n}^{3}+2n=$ {{field-4}}, where $b$ is {{field-5}}.\n\nTherefore, since ${n}^{3}+2n$ {{field-6}} a multiple of $2,$ we conclude that ${n}^{3}+2n$ is {{field-7}}."
